Feature: Databricks PySpark script to transfer eligible files from Vendor S3 bucket to Purgo S3 folder

  The script transfers files from the Vendor S3 folder to the Purgo S3 folder only if:
    - The file is listed in the Vendor S3 folder.
    - The file does NOT exist in either the Purgo S3 folder or the Archive S3 folder.
    - The file is marked as active ("A") in the purgo_playground.ingest_config_master table.
  The script retrieves S3 folder paths from ingest_config_master and uses Databricks secrets for AWS credentials.

  Background:
    Given Unity Catalog is set to "purgo_databricks"
    And Schema is set to "purgo_playground"
    And AWS credentials "access_key" and "secret_key" are retrieved from Databricks secret scope "aws_keys"
    And ingest_config_master table is available with columns: config_id, file_name, actual_file_name, s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, s3_archive_path, active_flag

  # Happy Path: File is eligible and transferred
  Scenario Outline: Transfer eligible active file from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "A"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" does not exist in Purgo S3 folder "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" does not exist in Archive S3 folder "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<actual_file_name>" is copied from "<s3_vendor_path>" to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" remains in "<s3_vendor_path>" (no deletion)
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" does not exist in "<s3_archive_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "success" for "<actual_file_name>"

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG001    | data1.csv      | data1.csv        | s3://vendor-bucket/folder1/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |
      | CFG002    | report2024.txt | report2024.txt   | s3://vendor-bucket/reports/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  # Error Path: File is not active
  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer inactive file from Vendor S3
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "<inactive_flag>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<actual_file_name>" is not copied to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "skipped" and message "File not active" for "<actual_file_name>"

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | inactive_flag |
      | CFG003    | data2.csv      | data2.csv        | s3://vendor-bucket/folder2/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | I            |
      | CFG004    | oldfile.txt    | oldfile.txt      | s3://vendor-bucket/old/       | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | N            |

  # Error Path: File already exists in Purgo S3
  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer file that already exists in Purgo S3
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "A"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Purgo S3 folder "<s3_landing_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<actual_file_name>" is not copied to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "skipped" and message "File already exists in Purgo S3" for "<actual_file_name>"

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG005    | data3.csv      | data3.csv        | s3://vendor-bucket/folder3/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |
      | CFG006    | report2023.txt | report2023.txt   | s3://vendor-bucket/reports/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  # Error Path: File already exists in Archive S3
  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer file that already exists in Archive S3
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "A"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Archive S3 folder "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<actual_file_name>" is not copied to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "skipped" and message "File already exists in Archive S3" for "<actual_file_name>"

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG007    | data4.csv      | data4.csv        | s3://vendor-bucket/folder4/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |
      | CFG008    | archive2022.txt| archive2022.txt  | s3://vendor-bucket/archives/  | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  # Error Path: File does not exist in Vendor S3
  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer file that does not exist in Vendor S3
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "A"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" does not exist in Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<actual_file_name>" is not copied to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "skipped" and message "File not found in Vendor S3" for "<actual_file_name>"

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG009    | missing.csv    | missing.csv      | s3://vendor-bucket/folder5/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |
      | CFG010    | lost.txt       | lost.txt         | s3://vendor-bucket/lost/      | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  # Validation: S3 path retrieval from ingest_config_master
  Scenario Outline: Retrieve S3 folder paths from ingest_config_master
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "A"
    When the script queries ingest_config_master for active_flag = "A"
    Then the script retrieves "<s3_vendor_path>" as Vendor S3 folder path
    And the script retrieves "<s3_landing_path>" as Purgo S3 folder path
    And the script retrieves "<s3_archive_path>" as Archive S3 folder path

    Examples:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG011    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder6/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |
      | CFG012    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder7/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  # Validation: Only files with active_flag = "A" are considered
  Scenario Outline: Filter files by active_flag in ingest_config_master
    Given ingest_config_master contains rows with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", active_flag "<flag>"
    When the script filters ingest_config_master for active_flag = "A"
    Then only files with active_flag "A" are considered for transfer

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | flag |
      | CFG013    | active.csv     | active.csv       | A    |
      | CFG014    | inactive.csv   | inactive.csv     | I    |
      | CFG015    | notactive.txt  | notactive.txt    | N    |

  # Validation: File existence check is case-sensitive
  Scenario Outline: File existence check is case-sensitive
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", active_flag "A"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<case_variant_file_name>" exists in Purgo S3 folder "<s3_landing_path>"
    When the script checks for file existence in Purgo S3
    Then the file "<actual_file_name>" is considered different from "<case_variant_file_name>" due to case sensitivity
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" is eligible for transfer

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | case_variant_file_name |
      | CFG016    | Data5.csv      | Data5.csv        | s3://vendor-bucket/folder8/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | data5.csv             |
      | CFG017    | Report2025.txt | Report2025.txt   | s3://vendor-bucket/reports/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | report2025.txt        |

  # Error Path: AWS credentials missing
  Scenario: Fail if AWS credentials are not available in Databricks secret scope
    Given Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" does not contain "access_key" or "secret_key"
    When the script is executed
    Then the script fails with error message "AWS credentials not found in Databricks secret scope 'aws_keys'"

  # Error Path: S3 path missing in ingest_config_master
  Scenario Outline: Fail if S3 folder path is missing in ingest_config_master
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "A"
    When the script queries ingest_config_master for S3 folder paths
    Then the script fails with error message "S3 folder path missing in ingest_config_master for config_id <config_id>"

    Examples:
      | config_id | s3_vendor_path | s3_landing_path | s3_archive_path |
      | CFG018    |                | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/ | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/ |
      | CFG019    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder9/ |                | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/ |
      | CFG020    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder10/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/ |                |

  # Error Path: File transfer failure
  Scenario Outline: Log error if file transfer fails
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "A"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" does not exist in Purgo S3 folder "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" does not exist in Archive S3 folder "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script attempts to transfer the file and the transfer fails due to "<error_reason>"
    Then the transfer is logged with status "error" and message "<error_reason>" for "<actual_file_name>"

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | error_reason                |
      | CFG021    | data6.csv      | data6.csv        | s3://vendor-bucket/folder11/  | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | S3 permission denied        |
      | CFG022    | report2026.txt | report2026.txt   | s3://vendor-bucket/reports/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | Network timeout             |
      | CFG023    | file7.txt      | file7.txt        | s3://vendor-bucket/folder12/  | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | Insufficient disk space     |

  # Validation: Only ingest_config_master is used for config and file selection
  Scenario: Only ingest_config_master is used for S3 path and active_flag filtering
    Given ingest_config_master contains configuration rows
    And other configuration tables exist in the schema
    When the script selects files and S3 paths for transfer
    Then only ingest_config_master is used for S3 path and active_flag filtering

  # Validation: File transfer is a copy, not a move
  Scenario Outline: File is copied, not deleted from Vendor S3
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "A"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" does not exist in Purgo S3 folder "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" does not exist in Archive S3 folder "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<actual_file_name>" is copied to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" remains in "<s3_vendor_path>"

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG024    | data8.csv      | data8.csv        | s3://vendor-bucket/folder13/  | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |
      | CFG025    | report2027.txt | report2027.txt   | s3://vendor-bucket/reports/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  # Validation: File selection is based on actual_file_name
  Scenario Outline: File selection and existence check use actual_file_name
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with config_id "<config_id>", file_name "<file_name>", actual_file_name "<actual_file_name>", s3_vendor_path "<s3_vendor_path>", s3_landing_path "<s3_landing_path>", s3_archive_path "<s3_archive_path>", active_flag "A"
    And the file "<actual_file_name>" exists in Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>"
    When the script checks for file existence in Purgo and Archive S3 folders
    Then the script matches files using "<actual_file_name>" only

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name      | actual_file_name | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG026    | data9.csv      | data9.csv        | s3://vendor-bucket/folder14/  | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |
      | CFG027    | report2028.txt | report2028.txt   | s3://vendor-bucket/reports/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |
